{
  "id": "s01-l02",
  "unit": "s01-vowels",
  "title": "Vowels 2: উ ঊ ঋ এ",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "- **উ** and **ঊ** are both `u` as in *food*, a 'short' and 'long' pair that **sound the same** in speech. The long ঊ has one more stroke.\n- **ঋ** is said `ri` as in *rip*. It mostly appears in words borrowed from Sanskrit, like ঋতু (season).\n- **এ** = `e`. It has two sounds: an open 'a' as in *cat* (এক `ek`, one; এখন `ekhon`, now) or 'ay' as in *say* (এই `ei`, this). You learn which by listening.\n\nWatch out: উ looks a lot like the consonant ড (`d`) that you'll meet later; ড has a notch in its top line.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "l-u",
      "bn": "উ",
      "tr": "u",
      "en": "u as in 'food' (short-u letter)",
      "notes": "Name: hroshsho-u (হ্রস্ব উ). Sounds the same as ঊ in modern speech."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-uu",
      "bn": "ঊ",
      "tr": "u",
      "en": "u as in 'food' (long-u letter)",
      "notes": "Name: dirgho-u (দীর্ঘ ঊ). Same sound as উ; it is উ with an extra loop on top-right. Rare at the start of words."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-ri",
      "bn": "ঋ",
      "tr": "ri",
      "en": "ri as in 'rip'",
      "notes": "Name: ri (ঋ). Historically a vowel; in modern Bengali it is simply said 'ri'. Found mostly in Sanskrit-origin words."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-e",
      "bn": "এ",
      "tr": "e",
      "en": "e as in 'bed' or 'ay' as in 'say'",
      "notes": "Name: e (এ). Two pronunciations; the word decides which (open æ in এক 'ack' and এখন 'ækhon'; 'ay' in এই 'ei')."
    },
    {
      "id": "ut",
      "bn": "উট",
      "tr": "ut",
      "en": "camel"
    },
    {
      "id": "ukil",
      "bn": "উকিল",
      "tr": "ukil",
      "en": "lawyer"
    },
    {
      "id": "uru",
      "bn": "ঊরু",
      "tr": "uru",
      "en": "thigh"
    },
    {
      "id": "usha",
      "bn": "ঊষা",
      "tr": "usha",
      "en": "dawn",
      "notes": "Also a common girl's name. Alphabet-chart word: ঊ-তে ঊষা."
    },
    {
      "id": "rishi",
      "bn": "ঋষি",
      "tr": "rishi",
      "en": "sage (wise holy man)"
    },
    {
      "id": "ritu",
      "bn": "ঋতু",
      "tr": "ritu",
      "en": "season",
      "notes": "Bengal traditionally has six seasons (ছয় ঋতু)."
    },
    {
      "id": "ek",
      "bn": "এক",
      "tr": "ek",
      "en": "one",
      "notes": "Pronounced like English 'ack' (open e)."
    },
    {
      "id": "ekhon",
      "bn": "এখন",
      "tr": "ekhon",
      "en": "now",
      "notes": "Pronounced with an open e, like 'ack-hon' (æ)."
    }
  ],
